Speculative drawing leaves no trace: begin_speculation and end_speculation

The port draws a step's in-between picture on the one renderer, before the
real chain, and the real chain must then start from exactly the state it
would have had without it (the port draws exactly what the game draws). Local
memory, as the shaders keep it, is more than the guest's VRAM: with
super-sampling it holds a copy of the single-rate values and one copy per sample.

GSInterface::begin_speculation() flushes, copies the whole of it aside on
the GPU (GSRenderer::save_vram_state) and starts a log of the pages that
rendering, HOST -> LOCAL transfers, LOCAL -> LOCAL copies and host writes
write (PageTracker::begin_write_log). end_speculation() flushes, copies
back from the aside copy exactly the pages in the log, in every slice
(GSRenderer::restore_vram_pages), marks them written so that the textures
cached from them are dropped, and puts the CLUT cache back: the instance
of the start is copied to a fresh one (the instances only move forward)
and the cache is rewound to it. Nothing is waited for on the CPU. The
registers, the GIF paths and what the caller keeps about them are the
caller's to put back.

GSInterface::rewind_speculation() does the copying back of end_speculation() and goes on with the speculation: the copy
made aside equals local memory again, so it is kept (not made again) and the log of pages starts afresh. A step
with several pictures begins once, rewinds between the pictures and ends once.

While a speculation is on (GSRenderer::set_speculation_sync), the command
buffer of each submission signals a semaphore that the next async transfer
submission waits for, and the generic queue waits for the async transfers at
the transfer stage too. The library orders the two queues only where shaders
read what the async queue wrote (host-to-local copies of single pages); a
restore that the generic queue ran late could overwrite what the async queue
had meanwhile copied for the real chain (seen as a wrong picture at one
step in 250,000, when the GPU was shared). The test knobs set_test_knobs
(a stall before the restore, and the ordering switched off) make that
race show at once.

Applied by tools/setup.sh and tools/setup.ps1 after patch 0004 to the
pinned paraLLEl-GS commit (tools/versions.txt). paraLLEl-GS is
LGPL-3.0-or-later; this patch is published with the port under the same
license.

